1
00:00:01,671 --> 00:00:04,440
(Crows cawing)

2
00:00:04,475 --> 00:00:06,809
<i>(Frankie) There are all
kinds of Valentine's gifts.</i>

3
00:00:06,843 --> 00:00:08,861
<i>Some are better than
others, but the best ones</i>

4
00:00:08,896 --> 00:00:11,030
<i>come straight from the heart.</i>

5
00:00:11,065 --> 00:00:13,950
Oh, my gosh. Brick!

6
00:00:13,984 --> 00:00:16,035
I love it.

7
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:18,371
So... pretty.

8
00:00:18,405 --> 00:00:19,939
I know I'm supposed to
wait till Valentine's Day,

9
00:00:19,973 --> 00:00:23,025
but I just couldn't. I think
it's some of my best work.

10
00:00:23,043 --> 00:00:24,160
And I think you'd be right.

11
00:00:24,194 --> 00:00:27,163
Oh, thank you so much, Brick.

12
00:00:27,197 --> 00:00:31,250
Oh. I am gonna cherish this forever.

13
00:00:33,203 --> 00:00:35,371
(Clatter)

14
00:00:35,389 --> 00:00:37,706
<i>(TV playing indistinctly) Hey, dad,
I know you're probably wondering</i>

15
00:00:37,725 --> 00:00:39,892
what I'm doing for Valentine's Day.

16
00:00:39,927 --> 00:00:41,544
I don't exactly have a date,

17
00:00:41,562 --> 00:00:42,545
and that could really bum me out,

18
00:00:42,563 --> 00:00:44,230
'cause last year was so great

19
00:00:44,264 --> 00:00:46,432
- 'cause I had Matt and everything.
- Your mom's in the kitchen.

20
00:00:46,483 --> 00:00:48,601
She told me you guys were in here.

21
00:00:48,652 --> 00:00:50,853
Anyway, the school is having a dance,

22
00:00:50,887 --> 00:00:53,222
and I signed up to be
on the cleanup committee.

23
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:54,524
I may not be in love,

24
00:00:54,558 --> 00:00:56,442
but I can still clean
up for people in love.

25
00:00:56,493 --> 00:00:58,778
Oh, my God. Nobody goes to that lame dance.

26
00:00:58,829 --> 00:01:00,997
You're just mad because your
girlfriend is out of town.

27
00:01:01,031 --> 00:01:02,615
She's at a wedding...
something you'll never be in.

28
00:01:02,666 --> 00:01:04,083
I suggest buying a wacky hat

29
00:01:04,118 --> 00:01:05,752
and starting your cat collection now.

30
00:01:05,786 --> 00:01:09,255
That's not even an insult. I love cats.

31
00:01:09,289 --> 00:01:13,092
So, dad, are you doing anything
for mom for Valentine's Day?

32
00:01:13,127 --> 00:01:15,878
<i>Anything romantic?</i>

33
00:01:15,912 --> 00:01:17,296
Ah, we're not those kind of people.

34
00:01:17,331 --> 00:01:18,431
But you have to do something,

35
00:01:18,465 --> 00:01:21,884
even if it's just writing her a note

36
00:01:21,918 --> 00:01:25,138
or sending a cute text telling
her how much you love her.

37
00:01:25,189 --> 00:01:28,107
Well, I'm doing something.
I'm taking the Christmas tree

38
00:01:28,142 --> 00:01:29,258
out to the curb without being asked.

39
00:01:31,895 --> 00:01:34,147
(School bell rings) This is it?

40
00:01:34,198 --> 00:01:37,150
I thought you said Boss Co.
would be in the black by now.

41
00:01:37,201 --> 00:01:38,401
Is black the good one or the bad one?

42
00:01:38,435 --> 00:01:39,535
Look, we really ate it,

43
00:01:39,570 --> 00:01:40,787
trying to get that
possum out of the garage.

44
00:01:40,821 --> 00:01:42,822
Between Darrin's stitches
and the rabies shots,

45
00:01:42,873 --> 00:01:44,240
we got hosed.

46
00:01:44,274 --> 00:01:45,792
I can still see those
pink eyes coming at me.

47
00:01:45,826 --> 00:01:48,795
That's it, dudes. We're broke.

48
00:01:48,829 --> 00:01:51,764
And we can't lay anybody
off, 'cause we're all bosses.

49
00:01:51,945 --> 00:01:54,914
How can we be so powerful and
powerless at the same time?

50
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:56,148
I can't believe you're breaking up with me

51
00:01:56,183 --> 00:01:58,484
- right before Valentine's Day.
- I'm sorry!

52
00:01:58,518 --> 00:02:00,503
Really, I don't know what else to say.

53
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:03,222
Well, thanks a lot. Now I
don't have a date to the dance.

54
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:06,342
I hate you! (Cries)

55
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:07,943
(All) Whoa.

56
00:02:07,978 --> 00:02:09,061
(Snaps fingers)

57
00:02:09,079 --> 00:02:11,330
Wait a sec. There's a lot of guys

58
00:02:11,364 --> 00:02:12,531
wanting to get out of relationships

59
00:02:12,549 --> 00:02:14,466
before Valentine's Day, right?

60
00:02:14,484 --> 00:02:16,301
That way, they can avoid
spending all that money

61
00:02:16,319 --> 00:02:18,504
and taking things to the next level.

62
00:02:18,538 --> 00:02:20,256
- Go on.
- I will.

63
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:21,273
Breaking up in person's horrible,

64
00:02:21,308 --> 00:02:22,575
and the text dump can be forwarded,

65
00:02:22,609 --> 00:02:25,377
<i>land you on the douche
list, so what if we did it?</i>

66
00:02:26,071 --> 00:02:27,472
Did what?

67
00:02:27,506 --> 00:02:30,625
What if guys paid us to break
up with the girls for them? Huh?

68
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:32,410
Boss Co. breakup service.

69
00:02:32,445 --> 00:02:34,679
(Both laughing)

70
00:02:34,714 --> 00:02:37,732
Okay. Explain it to me one more time.

71
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:50,019
Mother? Why is this in the trash?

72
00:02:50,053 --> 00:02:52,771
Oh! Thank God you found it!

73
00:02:52,806 --> 00:02:56,025
<i>I have been looking everywhere for that.</i>

74
00:02:56,059 --> 00:02:58,060
Uh-huh. You are a lousy liar.

75
00:02:58,094 --> 00:03:00,079
(Sighs) Okay. Here's the thing.

76
00:03:00,113 --> 00:03:01,430
You guys bring home a lot of stuff,

77
00:03:01,464 --> 00:03:03,883
and that's great, but
I can't keep everything,

78
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:06,385
and truthfully, this is not your best work.

79
00:03:06,419 --> 00:03:08,270
And yet you keep this picture Axl drew

80
00:03:08,305 --> 00:03:09,955
of two butts orbing in the earth.

81
00:03:09,973 --> 00:03:13,776
(Sighs) Are the butrronauts
still up there? (Clatter)

82
00:03:13,827 --> 00:03:15,227
(Sighs)

83
00:03:15,245 --> 00:03:18,180
Look, Brick, I didn't throw
everything of yours away.

84
00:03:18,215 --> 00:03:20,065
I saved the important stuff.

85
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:21,584
Oh. Where is it?

86
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:24,103
Put away in boxes.

87
00:03:24,137 --> 00:03:26,305
Can I see it? The years
have gone by so fast,

88
00:03:26,323 --> 00:03:28,207
I'd like to reminisce.

89
00:03:28,241 --> 00:03:29,208
(Whispers) Reminisce.

90
00:03:29,242 --> 00:03:30,426
That's fine.

91
00:03:30,477 --> 00:03:32,144
But you know, all the
current magazines are saying

92
00:03:32,178 --> 00:03:33,963
we should live in the present, so... 

93
00:03:33,997 --> 00:03:35,281
Find it.

94
00:03:35,315 --> 00:03:37,983
(Sue screaming)

95
00:03:38,018 --> 00:03:39,818
I've got a date to the dance!

96
00:03:39,853 --> 00:03:42,421
Oh! I'm not gonna be a loser after all.

97
00:03:42,455 --> 00:03:44,340
Oh, my God. I'm so relieved.
I can barely breathe.

98
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:45,391
So what happened?

99
00:03:45,425 --> 00:03:47,443
Well, I just got off the phone with Matt.

100
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:49,411
Turns out he broke up with Sheri.

101
00:03:49,446 --> 00:03:52,181
I knew it wouldn't last.
And he realized he missed me

102
00:03:52,215 --> 00:03:55,317
and loved me and couldn't live without me.

103
00:03:55,352 --> 00:03:57,820
And he asked if he could
have the honor of taking me

104
00:03:57,871 --> 00:03:59,938
to the Valentine's dance!

105
00:03:59,956 --> 00:04:01,207
(Screaming)

106
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:04,343
Oh, honey. That's so great.

107
00:04:04,377 --> 00:04:05,644
I'm gonna ride my bike over to Carly's

108
00:04:05,678 --> 00:04:07,780
and tell her all about it. Aah!

109
00:04:07,814 --> 00:04:08,847
(Door opens)

110
00:04:09,985 --> 00:04:11,652
(Door closes) (Gasps) Guess what, dad?

111
00:04:11,687 --> 00:04:13,421
I'm going to the dance after all!

112
00:04:13,455 --> 00:04:15,173
<i>Romantic, huh?</i>

113
00:04:15,207 --> 00:04:17,725
Oh, and I see the tree's still up.

114
00:04:17,776 --> 00:04:18,809
Just sayin'.

115
00:04:18,827 --> 00:04:21,045
Aah!

116
00:04:22,798 --> 00:04:25,466
So you are... Amanda, right? (Pen clicks)

117
00:04:25,501 --> 00:04:27,201
And you date Connor?

118
00:04:27,252 --> 00:04:28,686
Now this may seem abrupt... (Pen clicks)

119
00:04:28,721 --> 00:04:31,689
but now that you're both
seniors and going to college,

120
00:04:31,723 --> 00:04:34,825
he feels it's a natural time
to start seeing other people.

121
00:04:34,843 --> 00:04:36,894
- What?
- He's very much enjoyed your time together,

122
00:04:36,929 --> 00:04:39,230
but I'm afraid that time
has... come to an end.

123
00:04:39,264 --> 00:04:40,598
And he would've been here himself,

124
00:04:40,632 --> 00:04:42,683
but he thought this was for the best.

125
00:04:42,718 --> 00:04:45,019
I can't believe he's
doing this. What a jerk!

126
00:04:45,054 --> 00:04:46,521
Don't despair.

127
00:04:46,572 --> 00:04:49,574
You're a beautiful young lady
with lots of love ahead of you.

128
00:04:49,608 --> 00:04:51,476
Any guy would be lucky to have you.

129
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:54,595
Just not Connor.

130
00:04:56,949 --> 00:04:58,349
(Rustles)

131
00:04:59,635 --> 00:05:02,520
(Dog barking in distance)

132
00:05:06,991 --> 00:05:11,261
"I know I never say it, but
you're very special to me."

133
00:05:11,296 --> 00:05:12,729
(Beep)

134
00:05:16,334 --> 00:05:20,137
(Cell phone buzzes)

135
00:05:20,171 --> 00:05:23,974
"You're special to me, too." Jim?

136
00:05:34,502 --> 00:05:37,287
(Door closes)

137
00:05:37,305 --> 00:05:41,108
Ah, Jim, uh... hey,
listen, about that text... 

138
00:05:41,142 --> 00:05:44,144
Yeah. I was kinda wanting
to talk to you about it, too.

139
00:05:44,178 --> 00:05:45,929
Uh, no. We don't have to do that.

140
00:05:45,963 --> 00:05:48,598
See, uh, in fact, that text was... 

141
00:05:48,633 --> 00:05:50,150
The nicest thing anybody's ever done.

142
00:05:50,184 --> 00:05:51,918
I'll just say it.

143
00:05:51,953 --> 00:05:53,854
You're the best boss I've ever had, Mike.

144
00:05:53,888 --> 00:05:56,940
Uh, all right, then. Thanks.

145
00:05:56,991 --> 00:06:01,077
I've been... kinda going
through a rough patch lately,

146
00:06:01,095 --> 00:06:04,264
and you telling me I'm special
is just the boost I needed.

147
00:06:04,298 --> 00:06:05,432
Uh-huh.

148
00:06:05,466 --> 00:06:07,567
Yeah.

149
00:06:07,602 --> 00:06:09,736
I never told anyone this.

150
00:06:09,771 --> 00:06:12,606
But I've always had a hard time fitting in.

151
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:15,609
When you're a kid, all you
wanna do is belong, you know?

152
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,210
Sure.

153
00:06:17,245 --> 00:06:19,930
See, I started going bald
when I was in grade school.

154
00:06:19,964 --> 00:06:24,401
You ever see a 180-pound
12-year-old with a comb-over?

155
00:06:24,435 --> 00:06:27,254
(Exhales) It feels good just to say it.

156
00:06:27,288 --> 00:06:29,339
(Exhales deeply)

157
00:06:29,357 --> 00:06:30,524
I heard about your guys' service,

158
00:06:30,575 --> 00:06:31,625
and I wanna dump my girlfriend,

159
00:06:31,659 --> 00:06:32,793
but I don't wanna hurt her feelings.

160
00:06:32,964 --> 00:06:34,347
You've come to the right place, Evan.

161
00:06:34,382 --> 00:06:35,682
(Bell rings) What am I signing?

162
00:06:35,733 --> 00:06:37,300
Ah, it's a standard release form

163
00:06:37,318 --> 00:06:39,619
saying we're not liable
if anything goes wrong.

164
00:06:39,654 --> 00:06:42,589
And that if your ex is hot,
we, the members of Boss Co.,

165
00:06:42,623 --> 00:06:43,974
reserve the right to ask her out

166
00:06:44,008 --> 00:06:47,544
after the appropriate 7-day waiting period.

167
00:06:47,578 --> 00:06:50,096
Correction... 3-day waiting period.

168
00:06:50,147 --> 00:06:53,533
Sorry, Rachel, but Spencer
feels you two have grown apart.

169
00:06:53,568 --> 00:06:54,951
(Crying) It's never gonna work.

170
00:06:54,969 --> 00:06:58,722
(Sobbing)

171
00:06:59,756 --> 00:07:01,707
We're sorry, Miss Poltorak,
but Mr. Whiteman thinks

172
00:07:01,758 --> 00:07:03,642
you guys are looking for different things.

173
00:07:03,693 --> 00:07:05,277
You're too good for him anyway.

174
00:07:05,328 --> 00:07:06,328
Really?

175
00:07:06,363 --> 00:07:08,097
Definitely.

176
00:07:08,131 --> 00:07:09,732
Now could you go online
and take a brief survey

177
00:07:09,766 --> 00:07:12,234
saying you were broken up with
in a kind and courteous manner?

178
00:07:12,269 --> 00:07:13,552
Oh, and if you could take a moment

179
00:07:13,587 --> 00:07:16,522
to "like" us on Facebook,
that would also be great.

180
00:07:17,056 --> 00:07:18,557
<i>So Brick's stuff was missing,</i>

181
00:07:18,591 --> 00:07:21,242
<i>and knowing Brick, he
wasn't gonna let it go.</i>

182
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:22,410
<i>I learned my lesson.</i>

183
00:07:22,428 --> 00:07:24,896
<i>Next time I throw away
any more art projects,</i>

184
00:07:24,931 --> 00:07:26,815
<i>I'm using the dumpster
behind the mini-mart.</i>

185
00:07:26,849 --> 00:07:29,868
<i>Anyway, I was desperate,
and I knew what I had to do.</i>

186
00:07:29,902 --> 00:07:31,153
Hey, Nancy.

187
00:07:31,187 --> 00:07:34,306
Oh, hi, Frankie. Wanna
come in for a cinnamon bun

188
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:35,590
and watch Dr. Oz?

189
00:07:35,625 --> 00:07:37,425
Oh, no, thanks.

190
00:07:37,443 --> 00:07:38,944
Listen, this is kind of embarrassing,

191
00:07:38,978 --> 00:07:42,431
but I can't find any of
Brick's old art projects.

192
00:07:42,465 --> 00:07:43,899
I'm pretty sure Mike threw them all out.

193
00:07:43,933 --> 00:07:46,051
Men do the craziest things, huh?

194
00:07:46,265 --> 00:07:48,066
Tell me about it. Remember Ron's perm?

195
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:51,836
Ooh. Anyway, I was
wondering if I could borrow

196
00:07:51,887 --> 00:07:54,773
one of your kids' old projects
and pass it off as Brick's.

197
00:07:54,824 --> 00:07:57,042
Absolutely. Believe me, I get it.

198
00:07:57,076 --> 00:08:01,279
Three kids... no way you
can keep up with everything.

199
00:08:01,314 --> 00:08:03,198
(Click)

200
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:05,166
(Whirring)

201
00:08:05,201 --> 00:08:07,352
(Gasps)

202
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:09,237
(Singsongy) Hey, lookie what I found.

203
00:08:09,271 --> 00:08:11,923
(Normal voice) Brick's
centerpiece from Thanksgiving.

204
00:08:11,958 --> 00:08:13,658
There's no way in hell Brick made that.

205
00:08:13,693 --> 00:08:16,895
(Sighs) Damn it, and this
was the worst one, too.

206
00:08:17,676 --> 00:08:21,012
(Sighs) I can't believe I
threw away all my son's stuff.

207
00:08:21,046 --> 00:08:23,030
Seriously, what kind of a mother am I?

208
00:08:23,081 --> 00:08:25,599
According to Brick's school,
not actively involved.

209
00:08:25,634 --> 00:08:26,667
Well, they're right, Mike.

210
00:08:26,702 --> 00:08:28,819
I'm a terrible, terrible mother.

211
00:08:28,853 --> 00:08:33,491
Uh... what were the
buttronauts doing in the trash?

212
00:08:33,525 --> 00:08:35,743
Do you not understand what
the buttronauts represent?

213
00:08:35,777 --> 00:08:37,862
They represent butts in space.

214
00:08:37,896 --> 00:08:40,347
Show a little respect.

215
00:08:42,984 --> 00:08:45,820
(Whistle blows in distance)

216
00:08:46,794 --> 00:08:48,678
I'm a good guy, Mike.

217
00:08:48,713 --> 00:08:50,346
I bust my hump around here.

218
00:08:50,364 --> 00:08:51,614
Yeah. You work hard.

219
00:08:51,649 --> 00:08:52,816
When why didn't I get

220
00:08:52,850 --> 00:08:55,418
a sweet, heartfelt text
from you like Jim did?

221
00:08:55,453 --> 00:08:57,754
Oh, no. Look, Dave, that was... 

222
00:08:57,772 --> 00:09:00,189
I thought we were more than co-workers.

223
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:01,975
I thought we were friends.

224
00:09:02,009 --> 00:09:04,060
I mean, we watch games together.

225
00:09:04,095 --> 00:09:06,229
Your family's been to my church.

226
00:09:06,263 --> 00:09:08,415
I even fixed the hole in your kid's wall.

227
00:09:08,449 --> 00:09:12,152
Okay, fine. You are... 

228
00:09:12,186 --> 00:09:15,622
really valuable around here.

229
00:09:15,690 --> 00:09:17,207
Not feeling it.

230
00:09:18,709 --> 00:09:20,877
You're special to me, too.

231
00:09:23,047 --> 00:09:24,714
All right.

232
00:09:24,748 --> 00:09:26,049
There it is.

233
00:09:27,635 --> 00:09:29,803
Now bring it in for a hug. Come on.

234
00:09:29,854 --> 00:09:33,106
Okay.

235
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:34,891
All right.

236
00:09:43,252 --> 00:09:45,804
<i>With Valentine's Day only two days away,</i>

237
00:09:45,838 --> 00:09:48,156
<i>the Boss Co. breakup service was booming.</i>

238
00:09:48,190 --> 00:09:49,808
♪

239
00:09:49,842 --> 00:09:53,078
<i>And nobody knew who was gonna be next.</i>

240
00:09:54,931 --> 00:09:57,849
(Man) * I can't take you to heaven

241
00:09:57,884 --> 00:10:00,569
♪ I can't promise forever

242
00:10:00,603 --> 00:10:01,987
♪ whoa!

243
00:10:02,021 --> 00:10:05,590
- We got a runner!
- Now let's be grown-up about this.

244
00:10:05,625 --> 00:10:07,542
It'll all be over soon.

245
00:10:08,878 --> 00:10:12,414
(Panting)

246
00:10:12,448 --> 00:10:14,633
Aren't you tired of running, Emma?

247
00:10:14,667 --> 00:10:17,753
I'm sorry, but you plus Kyle
no longer equals forever.

248
00:10:17,787 --> 00:10:20,021
(Crying)

249
00:10:21,056 --> 00:10:25,192
So, Brick, listen,

250
00:10:25,227 --> 00:10:27,928
I've looked all over, but I
can't seem to find your stuff,

251
00:10:27,963 --> 00:10:30,064
so I'm just gonna be honest with you.

252
00:10:30,098 --> 00:10:31,732
I think your dad threw it out.

253
00:10:32,901 --> 00:10:34,034
Okay, look, I'm sorry.

254
00:10:34,068 --> 00:10:36,737
I really am. I don't know.

255
00:10:36,772 --> 00:10:38,672
Maybe it's 'cause you're the third kid,

256
00:10:38,707 --> 00:10:40,524
or our house isn't big enough,

257
00:10:40,575 --> 00:10:44,389
or I'm just a sucky parent,
but I don't have your stuff.

258
00:10:45,082 --> 00:10:47,049
You don't have Axl or Sue's stuff either?

259
00:10:47,084 --> 00:10:49,035
We're talking about you now.

260
00:10:49,069 --> 00:10:51,971
But the point is, stuff doesn't matter.

261
00:10:51,989 --> 00:10:54,807
What's important is the feeling
I had when you gave it to me.

262
00:10:54,841 --> 00:10:56,959
I'll never lose that.

263
00:10:57,010 --> 00:10:58,911
I see. So it's all gone.

264
00:10:58,946 --> 00:11:01,063
Nothing of mine made an
impression. Interesting.

265
00:11:01,098 --> 00:11:03,916
Because I distinctly remember
a ceramic sponge caddy

266
00:11:03,951 --> 00:11:05,735
that said "I hate housework."

267
00:11:05,786 --> 00:11:08,421
I'm sorry. Do you like housework?

268
00:11:08,455 --> 00:11:11,173
Because I think that would
be something you would keep.

269
00:11:11,208 --> 00:11:12,558
(Chair scrapes floor)

270
00:11:14,361 --> 00:11:15,928
(Door opens)

271
00:11:17,003 --> 00:11:18,336
I'm just gonna say it.

272
00:11:18,371 --> 00:11:20,772
I've been working here
longer than Jim or Dave.

273
00:11:20,806 --> 00:11:23,608
If anybody should get a
nice text, it should be me.

274
00:11:23,643 --> 00:11:26,778
What about me? You know, I
gave my hearing to this place!

275
00:11:26,812 --> 00:11:28,413
(Men speaking at once)

276
00:11:28,447 --> 00:11:31,149
He gets a text. I don't get a text.

277
00:11:31,183 --> 00:11:32,734
(Men continue speaking at once)

278
00:11:32,958 --> 00:11:37,245
Hey, hey. The text
wasn't even meant for Jim.

279
00:11:37,279 --> 00:11:38,563
Okay? It was supposed to go to my wife

280
00:11:38,614 --> 00:11:40,515
for Valentine's Day.

281
00:11:42,251 --> 00:11:46,688
Wait a minute. That's what
you texted your wife for v-day?

282
00:11:47,012 --> 00:11:49,147
(Chuckles) She's your lady.

283
00:11:49,181 --> 00:11:52,617
You gotta tell her you love her, man.

284
00:11:53,167 --> 00:11:57,065
I'm with Chuck. It sounds
like you have intimacy issues.

285
00:11:57,121 --> 00:11:58,989
You do throw up walls, Mike.

286
00:11:59,023 --> 00:12:01,892
You should talk to somebody.
Our insurance covers half.

287
00:12:01,926 --> 00:12:03,493
Hey, nobody's throwing up any walls.

288
00:12:03,528 --> 00:12:06,329
And for your information,
I didn't just send a text.

289
00:12:06,364 --> 00:12:07,864
I also took the Christmas
tree down to the curb

290
00:12:07,899 --> 00:12:09,332
without being asked.

291
00:12:09,366 --> 00:12:12,285
Hey, don't be afraid, man.

292
00:12:12,336 --> 00:12:15,255
Tonight, when you're on
your futon with your lady,

293
00:12:15,289 --> 00:12:16,640
- you just lay...
- No, no!

294
00:12:16,674 --> 00:12:18,658
That's it. Everybody back to work.

295
00:12:20,377 --> 00:12:22,863
Let's go. Thanks for your interest.

296
00:12:25,016 --> 00:12:26,533
Oh! (Laughs)

297
00:12:28,257 --> 00:12:30,826
(Sniffs) Man, I love America.

298
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:32,027
Now that I'm rich, I guess
I should finally start

299
00:12:32,061 --> 00:12:33,278
thinking about giving back.

300
00:12:33,312 --> 00:12:35,247
You know, maybe talk to
some loser kid at school

301
00:12:35,281 --> 00:12:37,082
or plant a bush in a park

302
00:12:37,116 --> 00:12:38,617
with a giant plaque with my name on it.

303
00:12:38,651 --> 00:12:41,269
(Laughs) Whoo!

304
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:44,456
Hey. What's wrong with you, dude?

305
00:12:44,474 --> 00:12:46,908
That breakup with Kelly McCarthy was awful.

306
00:12:46,959 --> 00:12:49,928
Totally blindsided her.
She cried her contacts out,

307
00:12:49,946 --> 00:12:51,696
and then I heard she failed a calculus test

308
00:12:51,731 --> 00:12:52,998
'cause she couldn't see.

309
00:12:53,032 --> 00:12:55,267
She might not get into college.

310
00:12:55,301 --> 00:12:57,235
I need a man's opinion.

311
00:12:57,253 --> 00:12:59,571
For the dance tonight, should
I wear my hair up or down?

312
00:12:59,605 --> 00:13:03,141
Over your face. You can weave it
into your braces so it'll stay.

313
00:13:03,176 --> 00:13:04,443
Up.

314
00:13:04,477 --> 00:13:07,612
Thanks. Mom says my forehead
is one of my best features,

315
00:13:07,630 --> 00:13:09,681
so... 

316
00:13:10,795 --> 00:13:14,164
Look, Sean, it's just
a business, all right?

317
00:13:14,199 --> 00:13:15,449
These girls are gonna
get broken up with anyway.

318
00:13:15,483 --> 00:13:18,269
If we didn't do it, somebody else would've.

319
00:13:18,303 --> 00:13:19,970
This way, we build a successful company,

320
00:13:20,005 --> 00:13:22,239
sell it to the Chinese,
buy some recording time,

321
00:13:22,274 --> 00:13:23,340
cut a hit album, rock the planet,

322
00:13:23,374 --> 00:13:24,975
then start a men's fragrance line.

323
00:13:24,993 --> 00:13:26,794
Yeah, but at what cost?

324
00:13:26,828 --> 00:13:28,546
I agree with Sean.

325
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:30,164
All this money is covered in tears.

326
00:13:30,198 --> 00:13:31,916
(Telephone ringing) Phone!

327
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:34,235
<i>- (Sue) So get it!
- No, you get it!</i>

328
00:13:34,269 --> 00:13:36,120
I'm getting ready! I'm
in a business meeting!

329
00:13:36,154 --> 00:13:38,205
- But you're closer!
- So?!

330
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:41,141
<i>- So get it!
- No, you get it!</i>

331
00:13:41,176 --> 00:13:42,176
(Answering machine beeps)

332
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:44,685
Uh, hi, Sue. This is Matt.

333
00:13:44,719 --> 00:13:46,219
Listen, Sue, I can't take you to the dance

334
00:13:46,254 --> 00:13:47,487
'cause Sheri and I got back together.

335
00:13:47,521 --> 00:13:49,289
So... hope you're good.

336
00:13:49,324 --> 00:13:51,992
<i>Again, not taking you to the dance.</i>

337
00:13:52,026 --> 00:13:53,060
Sorry. (Beep)

338
00:13:53,094 --> 00:13:54,978
(Answering machine clicks) Wow.

339
00:13:55,919 --> 00:13:58,671
He can't cancel day of.

340
00:13:58,705 --> 00:14:01,040
I mean, yeah, Sue's a dork,
but he knew that going in.

341
00:14:01,074 --> 00:14:02,558
This Matt guy sucks.

342
00:14:02,593 --> 00:14:03,893
Dude, you gotta tell her.

343
00:14:03,927 --> 00:14:05,661
Well, I can't tell her. She's my sister.

344
00:14:05,695 --> 00:14:08,297
What if she... cries or something?

345
00:14:08,331 --> 00:14:11,000
I can't comfort her. I think it's illegal.

346
00:14:11,034 --> 00:14:12,134
Well, don't look at me. I'm spent.

347
00:14:12,169 --> 00:14:14,320
I don't have another breakup in me.

348
00:14:15,973 --> 00:14:18,491
Fine. I'll do it.

349
00:14:18,525 --> 00:14:20,910
What's one more girl who doesn't like me?

350
00:14:22,396 --> 00:14:23,879
(Knock on door)

351
00:14:24,807 --> 00:14:26,691
Uh... hey, Sue.

352
00:14:26,726 --> 00:14:27,692
Hey, Darrin.

353
00:14:27,727 --> 00:14:29,294
Thanks for the hair recommendation.

354
00:14:29,328 --> 00:14:30,929
It does look better up.

355
00:14:30,963 --> 00:14:33,515
<i>So... </i>

356
00:14:33,566 --> 00:14:35,300
what do you think?

357
00:14:36,619 --> 00:14:37,853
You look really nice.

358
00:14:37,887 --> 00:14:39,604
Thank you.

359
00:14:39,639 --> 00:14:43,325
So... listen... about that phone call... 

360
00:14:43,359 --> 00:14:46,278
I don't know how else to do
this but to come out with it.

361
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:49,381
Matt's back together with
Sheri. He's a major jerk,

362
00:14:49,415 --> 00:14:52,167
and he's not coming to Orson
to take you to the dance.

363
00:14:52,201 --> 00:14:54,703
What?

364
00:14:54,737 --> 00:14:56,671
Please don't make me say it again.

365
00:14:56,706 --> 00:14:58,373
But... 

366
00:14:58,407 --> 00:15:00,075
Oh.

367
00:15:00,109 --> 00:15:03,195
This is so embarrassing.

368
00:15:04,019 --> 00:15:07,338
Oh. I bragged to everyone about
going to the dance with Matt.

369
00:15:07,372 --> 00:15:09,540
I'm really sorry, Sue.

370
00:15:09,574 --> 00:15:12,843
And I still have to go because
I'm on the cleanup committee,

371
00:15:12,894 --> 00:15:14,912
and I'm gonna have to walk in all alone

372
00:15:14,946 --> 00:15:17,031
and watch everyone having a good time

373
00:15:17,049 --> 00:15:20,785
while I mop up their
spills and cupcake sludge.

374
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:22,370
It's getting really hard to stay optimistic

375
00:15:22,404 --> 00:15:24,021
about this night!

376
00:15:24,056 --> 00:15:25,690
You don't have to walk in alone.

377
00:15:25,724 --> 00:15:26,924
I can take you.

378
00:15:26,975 --> 00:15:29,110
What?

379
00:15:29,144 --> 00:15:32,129
Thanks, but you don't wanna do that.

380
00:15:32,164 --> 00:15:36,617
I know seniors don't go to
the lame Valentine's dance.

381
00:15:36,652 --> 00:15:38,686
No, I want to.

382
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:41,389
It'll feel good to do
something nice for a change.

383
00:15:45,427 --> 00:15:48,362
<i>(The Chevin's "Beautiful World" playing)</i>

384
00:15:52,089 --> 00:15:56,827
Oh, this is all so beautiful.
I love mirror balls.

385
00:15:56,861 --> 00:15:59,412
Yeah, it does look nice.

386
00:15:59,447 --> 00:16:00,931
Hey, come on.

387
00:16:00,965 --> 00:16:02,499
Let's dance.

388
00:16:02,517 --> 00:16:03,683
(Sue) Yeah. Okay.

389
00:16:03,718 --> 00:16:05,218
<i>* Such a beautiful world</i>

390
00:16:05,253 --> 00:16:13,026
<i>* can't we all live as one in peace? *</i>

391
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:15,378
<i>* oh</i>

392
00:16:15,412 --> 00:16:16,897
<i>* it's such a beautiful world</i>

393
00:16:16,948 --> 00:16:18,281
(laughs)

394
00:16:18,299 --> 00:16:23,737
<i>* Can't we all live as one in peace? *</i>

395
00:16:23,788 --> 00:16:26,373
<i>*</i>

396
00:16:26,407 --> 00:16:27,424
<i>* oh</i>

397
00:16:27,458 --> 00:16:30,393
<i>* it's such a beautiful world</i>

398
00:16:30,428 --> 00:16:36,833
<i>* and if you want it,
you just have to believe *</i>

399
00:16:36,868 --> 00:16:38,418
<i>(Tv playing indistinctly)</i>

400
00:16:40,338 --> 00:16:43,808
Man, I never thought about
how we were hurting people.

401
00:16:43,842 --> 00:16:46,127
Ugh. What have we done?

402
00:16:46,161 --> 00:16:47,395
We're love hitmen.

403
00:16:47,429 --> 00:16:48,896
We made money off other people's pain.

404
00:16:48,930 --> 00:16:50,598
Oh, man! I wish we had a time machine

405
00:16:50,632 --> 00:16:53,234
so we could go back and undo everything.

406
00:16:53,268 --> 00:16:55,653
And it would be super cool
just to have a time machine.

407
00:16:55,704 --> 00:16:56,971
Super cool.

408
00:16:57,005 --> 00:16:58,605
(Sighs)

409
00:16:59,875 --> 00:17:01,442
(Snaps fingers) Hang on a sec.

410
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:04,078
What's the opposite of
breaking things apart?

411
00:17:04,112 --> 00:17:06,113
Well, the opposite of fission is fusion.

412
00:17:06,131 --> 00:17:07,982
Everybody knows that.

413
00:17:08,016 --> 00:17:11,469
Okay. So... what if we
practice some of that fusion

414
00:17:11,503 --> 00:17:13,737
and got one couple together tonight?

415
00:17:13,772 --> 00:17:15,556
Right. Get some isotopes together

416
00:17:15,590 --> 00:17:17,658
and wait for a reaction.

417
00:17:17,692 --> 00:17:19,960
<i>(Chuckles) Uh... yeah.</i>

418
00:17:19,978 --> 00:17:22,313
(Laughs)

419
00:17:22,347 --> 00:17:23,764
We're going out to find a couple

420
00:17:23,798 --> 00:17:26,267
and get them together to
undo all the evil we've done!

421
00:17:26,301 --> 00:17:30,304
(Frankie) Okay! Bring back milk!

422
00:17:37,747 --> 00:17:39,266
<i>So Axl and Sean tried to
get a couple together... </i>

423
00:17:39,267 --> 00:17:41,216
<i>a journey which led them to the one place</i>

424
00:17:41,250 --> 00:17:43,852
<i>seniors never go... the Valentine's dance.</i>

425
00:17:43,886 --> 00:17:48,089
Hey, Paige, you look really nice tonight.

426
00:17:48,107 --> 00:17:50,442
So, listen, uh, here's the thing.

427
00:17:50,476 --> 00:17:52,260
You and Wade seemed really good together,

428
00:17:52,278 --> 00:17:55,063
so maybe if you guys just talked, uh... 

429
00:17:55,097 --> 00:17:57,148
Beat it, jerkwads. Haven't you done enough?

430
00:17:57,199 --> 00:17:58,650
Ignore them, Paige.

431
00:17:58,701 --> 00:18:00,735
No, no, we're not like that
anymore. We wanna help now.

432
00:18:00,769 --> 00:18:03,371
Ha. Sure, you do. 'Cause
if you get us back together,

433
00:18:03,406 --> 00:18:06,241
then you can break us up
again and make even more money.

434
00:18:06,275 --> 00:18:08,493
Normally that would be very
sound business practice,

435
00:18:08,544 --> 00:18:11,112
but I promise you that's
not what we're trying to do.

436
00:18:11,130 --> 00:18:13,948
We just wanna undo all we
did and make you guys happy.

437
00:18:13,966 --> 00:18:18,286
You wanna make me happy? Let
me punch your stupid face!

438
00:18:18,304 --> 00:18:20,455
You know, there are chaperones here.

439
00:18:20,473 --> 00:18:22,841
(Girls speaking at once)

440
00:18:22,892 --> 00:18:25,810
We gotta get outta here. Look
at all the rings Becky's wearing.

441
00:18:25,845 --> 00:18:28,763
So... (Chuckles) let's... 
whoo! Look out. (Mutters)

442
00:18:28,797 --> 00:18:30,965
Run! Get 'em!

443
00:18:30,983 --> 00:18:34,352
(Girls shouting indistinctly)

444
00:18:34,403 --> 00:18:36,938
(Water running in faucet)

445
00:18:36,972 --> 00:18:38,306
(Clears throat)

446
00:18:38,444 --> 00:18:39,760
Happy Valentine's Day.

447
00:18:39,778 --> 00:18:45,533
Oh! Thank you. Oh, they're beautiful.

448
00:18:45,568 --> 00:18:49,621
And happy Valentine's Day back. Mwah.

449
00:18:49,655 --> 00:18:51,272
Well, I stuck to our usual plan

450
00:18:51,290 --> 00:18:53,074
and didn't get you anything.

451
00:18:53,108 --> 00:18:54,542
Mm, well, the guys at the quarry

452
00:18:54,577 --> 00:18:57,545
had some weirdly strong opinions
about what I should do for you

453
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:59,330
for Valentine's Day.

454
00:18:59,381 --> 00:19:02,000
Aw, well, tell them thanks from me.

455
00:19:03,969 --> 00:19:05,119
(Water resumes running)

456
00:19:05,137 --> 00:19:07,589
I know I don't say it enough, but... 

457
00:19:08,841 --> 00:19:09,924
You know... 

458
00:19:09,958 --> 00:19:13,595
Uh-huh. I do.

459
00:19:16,231 --> 00:19:20,351
<i>So... you talk to the
guys at work about me.</i>

460
00:19:20,402 --> 00:19:23,821
(Chuckles) Sometimes.

461
00:19:25,524 --> 00:19:28,860
You know, you don't have
to stay and help clean up.

462
00:19:28,911 --> 00:19:29,977
You've done enough.

463
00:19:29,995 --> 00:19:31,479
It's okay.

464
00:19:31,497 --> 00:19:33,164
I'm having a good time.

465
00:19:33,198 --> 00:19:34,532
Oh, yeah!

466
00:19:34,583 --> 00:19:35,700
Nothing but net!

467
00:19:35,751 --> 00:19:38,653
(Laughs)

468
00:19:38,671 --> 00:19:40,355
(Sue gasps)

469
00:19:40,389 --> 00:19:42,090
Sorry!

470
00:19:43,125 --> 00:19:46,210
(Both laughing)

471
00:19:47,513 --> 00:19:49,797
(Sighs)

472
00:19:49,831 --> 00:19:51,966
I still can't believe Matt ditched me.

473
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,852
Forget about Matt. He's a loser.

474
00:19:54,887 --> 00:19:56,170
Well, on the bright side,

475
00:19:56,188 --> 00:19:58,106
this is the second time he's dumped me,

476
00:19:58,140 --> 00:20:00,475
so I'll probably get over him faster.

477
00:20:00,509 --> 00:20:02,060
(Paper rustles)

478
00:20:04,313 --> 00:20:07,148
Hey, listen. I know you're a senior,

479
00:20:07,182 --> 00:20:10,118
and you guys don't usually
come to the Valentine's dance,

480
00:20:10,152 --> 00:20:12,853
but I really appreciate you coming with me.

481
00:20:12,871 --> 00:20:15,073
It was really nice of you.

482
00:20:20,496 --> 00:20:21,462
Truth is... 

483
00:20:21,497 --> 00:20:23,998
(Clatters)

484
00:20:24,032 --> 00:20:25,800
I didn't do it to be nice.

485
00:20:47,122 --> 00:20:49,157
<i>Dear Brick, I wanted to take a minute,</i>

486
00:20:49,191 --> 00:20:51,993
<i>on this day devoted to
love, to let you know</i>

487
00:20:52,044 --> 00:20:54,545
<i>that even though I may not be able to find</i>

488
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:59,383
<i>any of your art projects,
you are always in my heart.</i>

489
00:20:59,418 --> 00:21:02,286
<i>I'm sorry I'm the kind of
mom who's tired all the time,</i>

490
00:21:02,321 --> 00:21:05,122
<i>and I know I'm not the most
organized person in the world.</i>

491
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:07,008
<i>Maybe I'm lazy. I don't know.</i>

492
00:21:07,042 --> 00:21:09,927
<i>But here's the thing.
This is the mom you got.</i>

493
00:21:09,961 --> 00:21:13,314
<i>I'm not perfect. I'm
flawed... pretty darn flawed.</i>

494
00:21:13,348 --> 00:21:15,299
<i>But I hope you'll read
this and always remember</i>

495
00:21:15,317 --> 00:21:17,902
<i>that on Valentine's Day 2013,</i>

496
00:21:17,936 --> 00:21:21,606
<i>your mom wanted you to
know how much she loves you.</i>

497
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,291
<i>Happy Valentine's Day, sweetie.</i>

498
00:21:23,325 --> 00:21:26,694
<i>All my love forever. Mom.</i>

499
00:21:32,367 --> 00:21:34,318
(Turns on faucet)

500
00:21:34,353 --> 00:21:36,454
(Turns off faucet)

